config FIBRIL_CAN_NODE_SOLENOID
	bool
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_FIBRIL_FCAN_SOLENOID_ENABLED
	select GPIO
	help
	  Compiled whenever the devicetree describes the valves, which is also
	  what puts Solenoid instances into the schema. Describing the hardware
	  is the whole of adding this function to an image.

config FIBRIL_CAN_NODE_SOLENOID_MAX
	int "Solenoid instances to allocate for"
	default 8
	range 1 32
	depends on FIBRIL_CAN_NODE_SOLENOID
	help
	  The schema's max_count for Solenoid: how many instances the generated
	  code reserves state for. It is a ceiling, not a count. It never
	  reaches the schema blob, so the bus and the ROS graph see only the
	  valves the devicetree actually wires; overshooting costs one byte of
	  .bss per unused instance.

	  Raise it only for a board with more valves than this. Lowering it
	  below the devicetree's length fails the BUILD_ASSERT in solenoid.c.
